                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Sink or Skim is a challenging, well-thought out idea. It's a whole new perspective (literally) on platformers and puzzle games alike, though expect to be having a harder time with the mechanics than the puzzles. It took time for me to master all the mechanics: wall-running, wall-jumping, vaulting, spinning, and keeping momentum to not slow down and sink like the rock I am.\n\nDon't let the adorable faces and cutesy dialogue fool you, this game is hard as shit. The 3 worlds go by pretty fast if you get the hang of it but some challenges really required thought and routing before you make that initial leap off of land. The graphics and pace progress with quality as you go through the game, with a few moments of the third world taking me by surprise as beautiful, almost Journey-esque. It's easy to tell that a lot of care went into this game's visuals and music, as instruments fade in and out dynamically with your actions and location in the world.\n\nSink or Skim is absolutely worth its $5 price tag and stands as a message that new ideas are still present in 2018, and not every indie game from a passionate, talented novice developer has to be a deep, pretentious allegory or political statement. It's fluid, pretty, and held my attention for the entire playthrough.",
